# Raw M5 data is not redistributed (competition terms), and a full-scale local
# run writes hundreds of megabytes of derived tables. Anchored to the repository
# root with a leading slash: an unanchored "artifacts/" also matches
# deploy/artifacts/, which would silently exclude the committed bundle below.
/datasets/
/data/processed/
/data/raw/*
!/data/raw/README.md
/artifacts/
/models/

# The deployment bundle is the deliberate exception: a small development-mode
# build over 200 real M5 series, committed so the hosted app works straight from
# a clone rather than showing its "artifacts not built" panel. Excluded from it
# are the feature matrix (only the pipeline reads that, and it is by far the
# largest part) and the run logs.
/deploy/data/processed/features/
/deploy/artifacts/logs/

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.env
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
